<title>USA: SA Telecommunications restructures costs.</title>
<headline>SA Telecommunications restructures costs.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS, Texas 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>SA Telecommunications Inc said on Thursday that it was restructuring operations to more closely align expenses with revenues.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said it expected the plan to lower costs by roughly $450,000 a month beginning in September. Cuts were slated for costs of revenue and selling, as well as general and adminstrative expenses.</p>
<p>The company also said the plan involved a &quot;reduction in force&quot; and the closing of many outlying sales office. SA Telecommunications, which provides travel and debit cards and wireless services, did not specify how many jobs would be lost and no one was immediately available at the company to comment on potential job cuts.</p>
</text>
